From 95741a72a15657eff63b9eb09b2c18f7c191bf71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Nedoshovenko <nikita.nedoshovenko@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:27:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Warn on waiting FPVs and mines; stop merging contacts at
 different places
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A unit walking up to a ждун, a mine or a tripwire got no warning, because warnings fired only for side == hostile
and radio reports rarely say 'enemy' for these. Unidentified drones, mines, guns and snipers now warn too
(backend and map).

Two sightings were merged when within 75 m plus speed x time, so two tanks at two landmarks a minute apart became
one, and two waiting FPVs 150 m apart became one. Movement allowance is now zero for static or firing contacts,
capped at 100 m when nobody said it was moving, and at 600 m when it is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KG2RA2i89hGvASt44B7U7K
