From eddf8c581018b06655a1aa674c6c679ea3b846ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Nedoshovenko <nikita.nedoshovenko@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:47:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Place status: destroyed, damaged, blocked, reopened;
 battle replay
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

'Міст біля Ромашки знищено, проїзду нема' / 'the bridge near the Odeon is destroyed' / 'road blocked at ...' is
plotted as a persistent obstacle where it is (uk, ru, en, fr), without moving the reporter. A later report
updates the same marker (damaged, then destroyed); 'reopened' / 'проїзд відкрито' takes it off the map, and
rejecting that report puts it back. Obstacles never raise a threat warning.

data/demo_net_battle.jsonl + 'Replay battle' button: three teams, a blown bridge confirmed by a second station,
two waiting FPVs, a mine a team walks onto, a road blocked and reopened. tests/test_battle_script.py replays it.

