From 3269db33ae2eebeef7af1dd69839ed50c33ca7a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Nedoshovenko <nikita.nedoshovenko@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:10:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Rules path: negation, hearsay, two units per call, clock
 method, own drones
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found by reading through the offline rules with odd but realistic calls:
- 'no enemy at the Odeon', 'біля Сараю противника немає', 'біля Сараю чисто' and 'reported there yesterday' moved the
  speaker to that place, and the Ukrainian one painted an enemy there. They now plot nothing and move nobody.
- 'Сокіл на Сараї, я на Ромашці' put the speaker at Сарай. Each unit named now gets its own fix.
- 'наблюдаю' / 'бачу' with nothing named made an unlocated phantom contact.
- 'на Орієнтирі три, міну бачу': a sighting with no place of its own is where the speaker just said he is.
- 'стою возле Сарая, метрів п'ятдесят на північ' dropped the offset.
- Clock method ('на дванадцяту годину, двісті метрів'): a ring at that distance, since the net does not know which
  way the speaker faces. It used to fuzzy-match the hour to a place.
- 'наша пташка' / 'our drone' is friendly and warns nobody.
- /net/recording: one clip that fails speech-to-text no longer loses the rest. Whisper in Auto language gets the
  Ukrainian prompt on a Cyrillic net.
Benchmark (scripts.stress --offline, Paris and Irpin, train and holdout): unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KG2RA2i89hGvASt44B7U7K
